  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "A devout woodland people whose law is preached as shelter, kinship, and sacred restraint.",
    "one_paragraph": "Nemedran settlements are grown into old forests rather than carved from them, with shrines and meeting halls built around living trunks sworn under ancient covenant. Their priests judge disputes beneath bough-shadow, their elders keep long kin records, and even strangers are owed bread and roof in foul weather. They distrust reckless magic and needless bloodshed, believing every unruled impulse invites the dark things beyond the tree line."
